328
00:14:04,028 --> 00:14:07,293
for some girl that you just met who's probably not even going to show up!
/fɔːr ˌsʌm ˈɡɜːl ðæt juː ˈdʒʌst ˈmɛt ˌhuːz ˈprɑːbəbli ˌnɑːt ˈiːvən ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈʃoʊ ˈʌp/

329
00:14:07,369 --> 00:14:08,773
I mean, where is she, Ted, huh?
/aɪ ˈmiːn ˈwɛr ɪz ʃiː ˈtɛd ˈhʌ/

330
00:14:08,881 --> 00:14:10,186
Where's Robin?
/ˌwɛrz ˈrɑːbɪn/

331
00:14:12,245 --> 00:14:13,013
Hi.
/ˈhaɪ/

332
00:14:13,692 --> 00:14:14,712
Hi, Ron.
/ˈhaɪ ˈrɑːn/

333
00:14:23,452 --> 00:14:26,866
So, you threw all these parties for me?
/ˈsoʊ juː ˈθruː ˈɔːl ðiːz ˈpɑːrɾiz fɔːr ˌmiː/

334
00:14:27,154 --> 00:14:29,663
No. Oh, you thought that... no!
/ˈnoʊ ˈoʊ juː ˈθɔːt ˈðæt ˈnoʊ/

335
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:31,726
I... okay, yes. You got me.
/ˈaɪ oʊˈkeɪ ˈjɛs juː ˈɡɑːt ˌmiː/

336
00:14:31,897 --> 00:14:36,523
One of the reasons I threw these parties was so that I could introduce you
/ˈwʌn ʌvðə ˈriːzənz aɪ ˈθruː ðiːz ˈpɑːrɾiz wʌz ˌsoʊ ðæt aɪ kʊd ˌɪntrəˈduːs juː/

337
00:14:36,611 --> 00:14:38,976
to, um, this guy.
/ˈtuː ˈʌm ðɪs ˈɡaɪ/

338
00:14:39,058 --> 00:14:42,222
Uh, I figured, you know, since it didn't work out between us
/ˈʌ aɪ ˈfɪɡɚd juː ˈnoʊ ˈsɪns ɪt ˈdɪdnt ˈwɜːk ˈaʊt bɪˈtwiːn ˌʌs/

339
00:14:42,288 --> 00:14:44,112
and now we can just laugh about it...
/ænd ˈnaʊ wiː kæn ˈdʒʌst ˈlæf ɐˈbaʊt ɪt/

340
00:14:45,521 --> 00:14:47,749
Anyway, Robin, this is...
/ˈɛnɪˌweɪ ˈrɑːbɪn ðɪs ˈɪz/

341
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:48,924
Carlos.
/ˈkɑːrloʊz/

342
00:14:49,421 --> 00:14:51,053
- Oh!
- Oh!

343
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:56,368
She's still talking to Carlos.
/ʃiːz ˈstɪl ˈtɔːkɪŋ tə ˈkɑːrloʊz/

344
00:14:56,850 --> 00:14:59,073
I can still win this. I-it's not over.
/aɪ kæn ˈstɪl ˈwɪn ˈðɪs aɪɪts ˌnɑːt ˈoʊvɚ/

345
00:14:59,168 --> 00:15:01,864
Okay, buddy. Time for the tough talk.
/oʊˈkeɪ ˈbʌdi ˈtaɪm fɚðə ˈtʌf ˈtɔːk/

346
00:15:02,032 --> 00:15:04,807
Robin seems great, but let's look at the facts.
/ˈrɑːbɪn ˈsiːmz ˈɡreɪt ˌbʌt ˈlɛts ˈlʊk æt ðə ˈfækts/

347
00:15:04,884 --> 00:15:06,322
You want to get married.
/juː ˈwɑːnt tə ɡɛt ˈmærid/

348
00:15:06,372 --> 00:15:10,869
And right now, there's a million women in New York looking for exactly you.
/ænd ˈraɪt ˈnaʊ ðɛrz ɐ ˈmɪliən ˈwɪmɪn ɪn ˈnuː ˈjɔːrk ˈlʊkɪŋ fɔːr ɛˈɡzæktli juː/

349
00:15:10,926 --> 00:15:12,430
But Robin ain't one of them.
/ˌbʌt ˈrɑːbɪn ˈeɪnt ˈwʌn ʌv ˌðɛm/

350
00:15:12,496 --> 00:15:15,159
She's not just one of them. She's the one.
/ʃiːz ˌnɑːt ˈdʒʌst ˈwʌn ʌv ˌðɛm ʃiːz ðə ˈwʌn/

351
00:15:15,241 --> 00:15:18,396
Yeah, well, the one is heading up to the roof.
/ˈjɛh ˈwɛl ðə ˈwʌn ɪz ˈhɛdɪŋ ˌʌp tə ðə ˈruːf/

352
00:15:20,986 --> 00:15:22,424
What are you going to do?
/ˌwʌt ɑːr juː ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈduː/

353
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,196
Nothing.
/ˈnʌθɪŋ/

354
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:28,138
It's a game. I got to just keep playing it.
/ɪts ɐ ˈɡeɪm aɪ ɡɑːt tə ˈdʒʌst ˈkiːp ˈpleɪɪŋ ɪt/

355
00:16:07,001 --> 00:16:07,906
Ted...
/ˈtɛd/

356
00:16:07,998 --> 00:16:10,168
Hey, Carlos, can you give us a minute?
/ˈheɪ ˈkɑːrloʊz kæn juː ˈɡɪv ˌʌs ɐ ˈmɪnɪt/

357
00:16:10,231 --> 00:16:12,282
Hey, no sweat, hombre.
/ˈheɪ ˈnoʊ ˈswɛt ˈhɑːmbɚ/

358
00:16:13,001 --> 00:16:13,865
See ya.
/ˈsiː jɐ/

359
00:16:17,691 --> 00:16:18,612
Robin...
/ˈrɑːbɪn/

360
00:16:18,873 --> 00:16:21,704
look, I didn't throw this party to set you up with Carlos,
/ˈlʊk aɪ ˈdɪdnt ˈθroʊ ðɪs ˈpɑːrɾi tə ˈsɛt juː ˌʌp wɪð ˈkɑːrloʊz/

361
00:16:21,771 --> 00:16:23,036
or the one before that,
/ɔːr ðə ˈwʌn bɪˌfoːr ˈðæt/

362
00:16:23,425 --> 00:16:24,827
or the one before that.
/ɔːr ðə ˈwʌn bɪˌfoːr ˈðæt/

363
00:16:26,139 --> 00:16:28,841
I threw these parties because I wanted to see you.
/aɪ ˈθruː ðiːz ˈpɑːrɾiz bɪˈkʌz aɪ ˈwɑːntᵻd tə ˈsiː juː/

364
00:16:29,850 --> 00:16:31,340
Well, here I am.
/ˈwɛl ˈhɪr aɪˈæm/

365
00:16:32,712 --> 00:16:35,728
There's something here, look, unless I'm crazy.
/ðɛrz ˈsʌmθɪŋ ˈhɪr ˈlʊk ʌˈnlɛs aɪm ˈkreɪzi/

366
00:16:36,239 --> 00:16:37,919
You're not crazy.
/jʊr ˌnɑːt ˈkreɪzi/

367
00:16:39,399 --> 00:16:41,088
I don't know, Ted.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈnoʊ ˈtɛd/

368
00:16:41,141 --> 00:16:43,306
I mean, we barely know each other
/aɪ ˈmiːn wiː ˈbɛrli ˈnoʊ ˈiːtʃ ˈʌðɚ/

369
00:16:43,521 --> 00:16:46,598
and you're looking at me with that look. And, it's like...
/ænd jʊr ˈlʊkɪŋ æt ˌmiː wɪð ðæt ˈlʊk ˈænd ɪts ˈlaɪk/

370
00:16:46,722 --> 00:16:47,489
Like, like what?
/ˈlaɪk ˈlaɪk ˈwʌt/

371
00:16:47,602 --> 00:16:50,509
Like, "Let's fall in love and get married
/ˈlaɪk ˈlɛts ˈfɔːl ɪn ˈlʌv ænd ɡɛt ˈmærid/

372
00:16:50,566 --> 00:16:52,941
and have kids and drive them to soccer practice."
/ænd hæv ˈkɪdz ænd ˈdraɪv ˌðɛm tə ˈsɑːkɚ ˈpræktɪs/

373
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:55,558
I'm not going to force sports on them unless they're interested.
/aɪm ˌnɑːt ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈfoːrs ˈspoːrts ˌɑːn ˌðɛm ʌˈnlɛs ðeɪɚr ˈɪntrəstᵻd/

374
00:16:57,217 --> 00:16:58,569
It's a great look.
/ɪts ɐ ˈɡreɪt ˈlʊk/

375
00:16:59,219 --> 00:17:00,749
But you're looking at the wrong girl.
/ˌbʌt jʊr ˈlʊkɪŋ æt ðə ˈrɔŋ ˈɡɜːl/

376
00:17:00,817 --> 00:17:02,473
- No, I'm not.
- Yes, you are.

377
00:17:02,557 --> 00:17:05,168
I don't want to get married right now, maybe ever.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈwɑːnt tə ɡɛt ˈmærid ˈraɪt ˈnaʊ ˈmeɪbiː ˈɛvɚ/

378
00:17:05,234 --> 00:17:11,644
And, if we got together, I'd feel like I'd either have to marry you or break your heart, and...
/ˈænd ɪf wiː ɡɑːt təˈɡɛðɚ aɪd ˈfiːl ˈlaɪk aɪd ˈiːðɚ hæv tə ˈmæri juː ɔːr ˈbreɪk jʊr ˈhɑːrt ˈænd/

379
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:15,326
I just couldn't do either of those things.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst ˌkʊdənt ˈduː ˈiːðɚr ʌv ðoʊz ˈθɪŋz/

380
00:17:15,818 --> 00:17:18,399
Just like you can't turn off the way you feel.
/ˈdʒʌst ˈlaɪk juː ˈkænt ˈtɜːn ˈɔf ðə ˈweɪ juː ˈfiːl/

381
00:17:21,772 --> 00:17:22,908
Click.
/ˈklɪk/

382
00:17:23,109 --> 00:17:24,634
Off. Let's make out.
/ˈɔf ˈlɛts ˌmeɪk ˈaʊt/

383
00:17:24,799 --> 00:17:25,767
What?
/ˈwʌt/

384
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:28,762
What? That was the off switch.
/ˈwʌt ðæt wʌzðɪ ˈɔf ˈswɪtʃ/

385
00:17:28,966 --> 00:17:30,353
And I turned it off.
/ænd aɪ ˈtɜːnd ɪɾ ˈɔf/

386
00:17:30,559 --> 00:17:34,583
I mean, look, sure, yes, I want to fall in love, get married, blah, blah, blah.
/aɪ ˈmiːn ˈlʊk ˈʃʊr ˈjɛs aɪ ˈwɑːnt tə ˈfɔːl ɪn ˈlʌv ɡɛt ˈmærid ˈblɑː ˈblɑː ˈblɑː/

387
00:17:34,650 --> 00:17:38,858
But, on the other hand... you, me,
/ˈbʌt ɑːnðɪ ˈʌðɚ ˈhænd ˈjuː ˈmiː/

388
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,926
the roof.
/ðə ˈruːf/

389
00:17:42,268 --> 00:17:43,820
There's no off switch.
/ðɛrz ˈnoʊ ˈɔf ˈswɪtʃ/

390
00:17:44,732 --> 00:17:46,322
There is an off switch.
/ðɛr ɪz ɐn ˈɔf ˈswɪtʃ/

391
00:17:47,136 --> 00:17:48,474
And it's off.
/ænd ɪts ˈɔf/

392
00:17:48,975 --> 00:17:50,245
No, it's not.
/ˈnoʊ ɪts ˈnɑːt/

393
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:52,805
Yes, it is.
/ˈjɛs ɪɾ ˈɪz/

394
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:54,721
No, it's not.
/ˈnoʊ ɪts ˈnɑːt/

395
00:17:54,781 --> 00:17:57,839
Yes... it is.
/ˈjɛs ɪɾ ˈɪz/

396
00:18:12,055 --> 00:18:13,362
No, it's not.
/ˈnoʊ ɪts ˈnɑːt/

397
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,639
You're right. There's no off switch.
/jʊr ˈraɪt ðɛrz ˈnoʊ ˈɔf ˈswɪtʃ/

398
00:18:17,995 --> 00:18:20,111
God, I wish there was an off switch!
/ˈɡɑːd aɪ ˈwɪʃ ðɛˌrwʌz ɐn ˈɔf ˈswɪtʃ/

399
00:18:20,883 --> 00:18:22,170
Me, too.
/ˈmiː ˈtuː/

400
00:18:27,489 --> 00:18:29,412
So, um...
/ˈsoʊ ˈʌm/

401
00:18:30,694 --> 00:18:32,244
What do we do now?
/ˌwʌt ˈduː wiː ˈduː ˈnaʊ/

402
00:18:34,964 --> 00:18:36,356
We could be friends.
/wiː kʊd biː ˈfrɛndz/

403
00:18:36,627 --> 00:18:37,831
Oh...
/ˈoʊ/

404
00:18:39,208 --> 00:18:43,924
Look, I know it sounds insincere when people say that, but...
/ˈlʊk aɪ ˈnoʊ ɪt ˈsaʊndz ˌɪnsɪˈnsɪr wɛn ˈpiːpəl ˈseɪ ˈðæt ˈbʌt/

405
00:18:44,526 --> 00:18:45,638
we could.
/wiː ˈkʊd/

406
00:18:46,474 --> 00:18:47,964
I don't know, Robin.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈnoʊ ˈrɑːbɪn/

407
00:18:48,133 --> 00:18:49,853
I've made such a jackass of myself here.
/aɪv ˌmeɪd ˈsʌtʃ ɐ ˈdʒækæs ʌv maɪˈsɛlf ˈhɪr/

408
00:18:49,914 --> 00:18:54,200
We start hanging out, every time I see you it'll be like, "Oh, that's right. I'm a jackass."
/wiː ˈstɑːrt ˈhæŋɪŋ ˈaʊt ˈɛvri ˈtaɪm aɪ ˈsiː juː ˌɪɾəl biː ˈlaɪk ˈoʊ ðæts ˈraɪt aɪm ɐ ˈdʒækæs/

409
00:18:54,609 --> 00:18:55,950
You're not a jackass.
/jʊr ˌnɑːɾə ˈdʒækæs/

410
00:18:56,591 --> 00:18:58,879
Look, I'm sorry. I only moved here in April
/ˈlʊk aɪm ˈsɔːri aɪ ˈoʊnli ˈmuːvd ˈhɪr ɪn ˈeɪprəl/

411
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,455
and I'm always working and
/ænd aɪm ˈɔːlweɪz ˈwɜːkɪŋ ænd/

412
00:19:01,737 --> 00:19:04,864
I just haven't met a lot of good people so far.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst ˈhævənt ˈmɛt ɐ ˈlɑːt ʌv ˈɡʊd ˈpiːpəl ˈsoʊ ˌfɑːr/

413
00:19:06,237 --> 00:19:07,655
But I understand.
/ˌbʌt aɪ ˌʌˈndɚstænd/

414
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:13,829
Well, uh, maybe in a few months, after it's not so fresh,
/ˈwɛl ˈʌ ˈmeɪbiː ɪn ɐ ˈfjuː ˈmʌnθs ˈæftɚr ɪts ˌnɑːt ˌsoʊ ˈfrɛʃ/

415
00:19:13,904 --> 00:19:17,844
we could all, uh, you know, get a beer.
/wiː kʊd ˈɔːl ˈʌ juː ˈnoʊ ɡɛt ɐ ˈbɪr/

416
00:19:18,376 --> 00:19:19,462
Yeah.
/ˈjɛh/

417
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:21,832
That sounds good.
/ðæt ˈsaʊndz ˈɡʊd/

418
00:19:23,266 --> 00:19:24,731
I'll see you, Ted.
/aɪl ˈsiː juː ˈtɛd/

419
00:19:29,933 --> 00:19:31,924
Or, you know, now.
/ˈɔːr juː ˈnoʊ ˈnaʊ/

420
00:19:35,621 --> 00:19:38,170
We could all get a beer now.
/wiː kʊd ˈɔːl ɡɛt ɐ ˈbɪr ˈnaʊ/

421
00:19:41,181 --> 00:19:42,493
I'd like that.
/aɪd ˈlaɪk ˈðæt/

422
00:19:44,963 --> 00:19:49,317
My friends are going to love you... like you, you know, as a friend.
/maɪ ˈfrɛndz ɑːr ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈlʌv juː ˈlaɪk juː juː ˈnoʊ æz ɐ ˈfrɛnd/

423
00:19:50,685 --> 00:19:51,948
Jackass.
/ˈdʒækæs/

424
00:19:54,703 --> 00:19:56,116
Unbelievable.
/ʌnbɪˈliːvəbəl/

425
00:19:56,669 --> 00:19:59,773
That's just a recipe for disaster. They work together!
/ðæts ˈdʒʌst ɐ ˈrɛsɪˌpiː fɔːr dɪˈzæstɚ ðeɪ ˈwɜːk təˈɡɛðɚ/

426
00:19:59,849 --> 00:20:00,739
Are you jealous?
/ɑːr juː ˈdʒɛləs/

427
00:20:00,821 --> 00:20:04,116
Oh, please. What does Carlos have that I don't?
/ˈoʊ ˈpliːz ˌwʌt ˈdʌz ˈkɑːrloʊz hæv ðæt aɪ ˈdoʊnt/

428
00:20:04,123 --> 00:20:06,423
- A date tonight.
- Oh!

429
00:20:06,495 --> 00:20:08,420
Stop the tape. Rewind. Play it again.
/ˈstɑːp ðə ˈteɪp rɪˈwaɪnd ˈpleɪ ɪɾ ɐˈɡɛn/

430
00:20:08,699 --> 00:20:11,435
- A date tonight.
- Oh!

431
00:20:11,578 --> 00:20:12,895
I'm not sure I like her.
/aɪm ˌnɑːt ˈʃʊr aɪ ˈlaɪk hɜː/

432
00:20:13,779 --> 00:20:15,361
Hey, don't you have a paper to write?
/ˈheɪ ˈdoʊnt juː hæv ɐ ˈpeɪpɚ tə ˈraɪt/

433
00:20:15,435 --> 00:20:17,952
- Dude, you're talking to the kid.
- I know it.

434
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:19,607
I'm going to knock back this beer.
/aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈnɑːk ˈbæk ðɪs ˈbɪr/

435
00:20:19,679 --> 00:20:21,552
I'm going to knock back one more beer.
/aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈnɑːk ˈbæk ˈwʌn ˈmoːr ˈbɪr/

436
00:20:21,615 --> 00:20:24,547
I'm going to go home. I'm going to write a 25-page paper.
/aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˌɡoʊ ˈhoʊm aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈraɪt ɐ ˈtwɛnti ˈfaɪˈvpeɪdʒ ˈpeɪpɚ/

437
00:20:24,634 --> 00:20:26,836
I'm going to hand it in and I'm going to get an "A."
/aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈhænd ɪɾ ɪn ænd aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ɡɛt æn ˈeɪ/

438
00:20:26,908 --> 00:20:30,308
My name is Rufus and that's the trufus.
/maɪ ˈneɪm ɪz ˈruːfəs ænd ðæts ðə ˈtruːfəs/

439
00:20:30,742 --> 00:20:32,125
He got a B-minus.
/hiː ɡɑːt ɐ ˈbiˈːmaɪnəs/

440
00:20:32,202 --> 00:20:35,177
But still, 25 pages in one night, B-minus?
/ˌbʌt ˈstɪl ˈtwɛnti ˈfaɪv ˈpeɪdʒɪz ɪn ˈwʌn ˈnaɪt ˈbiˈːmaɪnəs/

441
00:20:35,228 --> 00:20:36,576
The kid was good.
/ðə ˈkɪd wʌz ˈɡʊd/

442
00:20:37,102 --> 00:20:38,855
At least let me buy you a beer.
/æt ˈliːst ˈlɛt ˌmiː ˈbaɪ juː ɐ ˈbɪr/

443
00:20:38,935 --> 00:20:40,532
Come on, I'll buy everyone a beer.
/ˈkʌm ˈɑːn aɪl ˈbaɪ ˈɛvrɪˌwʌn ɐ ˈbɪr/

444
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:41,669
I'll help carry.
/aɪl ˈhɛlp ˈkæri/

445
00:20:46,881 --> 00:20:48,290
- You know something Ted?
- What?

446
00:20:48,335 --> 00:20:49,574
You are a catch.
/juː ɑːr ɐ ˈkætʃ/

447
00:20:49,677 --> 00:20:52,195
You're going to make some girl very happy.
/jʊr ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˌmeɪk ˌsʌm ˈɡɜːl ˈvɛri ˈhæpi/

448
00:20:52,386 --> 00:20:55,186
And I am going to help you find her.
/ænd aɪɐm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈhɛlp juː ˈfaɪnd hɜː/

449
00:20:55,529 --> 00:20:57,188
Well, good luck.
/ˈwɛl ˈɡʊd ˈlʌk/

450
00:20:57,470 --> 00:20:59,412
I mean, maybe New York's just too big a town.
/aɪ ˈmiːn ˈmeɪbiː ˈnuː ˈjɔːrks ˈdʒʌst ˈtuː ˈbɪɡ ɐ ˈtaʊn/

451
00:20:59,461 --> 00:21:01,515
I mean, there's millions of people in this city.
/aɪ ˈmiːn ðɛrz ˈmɪliənz ʌv ˈpiːpəl ɪn ðɪs ˈsɪɾi/

452
00:21:01,632 --> 00:21:04,730
How, in all this mess, is a guy supposed to find the love of his life?
/ˈhaʊ ɪn ˈɔːl ðɪs ˈmɛs ɪz ɐ ˈɡaɪ sʌˈpoʊzd tə ˈfaɪnd ðə ˈlʌv ʌv hɪz ˈlaɪf/

453
00:21:04,796 --> 00:21:07,361
